# project.json's docs URL; changes with D4.
docs/README.md	You can read this tree here on GitHub or as a site — [docs.switchboard.coreplanelabs.dev](https://docs.switchboard.coreplanelabs.dev), also reachable at `/docs` on the dashboard and from the docs icon in its header. Same markdown, same links: the site is compiled from these files on every push, with search, diagrams, and dark mode.

# `op://` is 1Password's own reference scheme — the shape the `configSource` / `secretsSource` integration speaks — not one of our vault paths.
docs/decisions/0001-seams-with-two-implementations.md	| Config source | path, `github://`, `op://` |
docs/how-to/deploy-and-rotate-a-secret.md	# the value comes from the profile's secretsSource (~/.secrets/switchboard/<NAME> by default, or op://Vault/Item)
docs/how-to/operate-production.md	`configSource` is where the bot's config comes from: a path (the default), `github://owner/repo/path@ref` read with `CONFIG_REPO_TOKEN`, or `op://Vault/Item/field` read with the 1Password CLI and `OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN`. The image carries no config. `deploy all` reads and validates the config before any Worker deploys and, right before the bot step, pushes it as the `base` document on the state Worker (with `MEMORY_TOKEN`); the bot's container reads that document when it starts (`SWITCHBOARD_CONFIG=state://base`). A config change without a release is `npm run cli -- deploy config` (the profile's source, or `--source <path|github://…|op://…>`) followed by `npm run cli -- deploy restart` — the running container keeps the config it started with, exactly as it keeps its secrets. An unreadable source, a config that does not validate, or a missing `MEMORY_TOKEN` refuses before anything changes.
docs/how-to/operate-production.md	`secretsSource` is where `deploy secrets <worker>` (`npm run secrets` in each Worker's directory) reads the values of the secrets `deploy/secrets.manifest.json` lists for that Worker: a directory of `<NAME>` files (`~/.secrets/switchboard` when the profile names none) or a 1Password item, `op://Vault/Item`, with one field per secret name (needs `OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN` or an `op signin` session). The command asks the source once which names it holds and refuses before any upload when a required one is absent; each value goes to `wrangler secret put` on stdin and is never printed. A shared bearer must be put on every Worker the manifest lists for it, and a bot secret is live only after `deploy restart`.

# Generated from the command registry by `docs:gen`: the `deploy secrets` and `env bootstrap` descriptions name 1Password as the integration they speak to, not a vault path.
docs/reference/cli.md	| `deploy secrets <memory\|bot\|resident\|sandbox> [--only <string>]` | Put a Worker's secrets from the deployment profile's secretsSource (a directory of &lt;NAME&gt; files, or an op://Vault/Item): every name deploy/secrets.manifest.json lists for it, refused before any upload when a required value is absent. Values ride stdin into `wrangler secret put`; none is ever printed. | CLI only |
docs/reference/cli.md	| `env bootstrap --env <string> --service <string> [--apply] [--out <string>] [--manifest <string>]` | Populate the agent's execution environment with a downstream service's UAT env vars from 1Password (dry-run unless --apply). | CLI only |

